0000:              ; 		Will not use any string space since
0000:              ; 		The string descriptor  will point into the
0000:              ; 		Program itself. in general, copying is done
0000:              ; 		When a string value is in "BUF", or it is in string
0000:              ; 		Space and there is an active pointer to it.
0000:              ; 		Thus f$=g$ will cause copying IF g$ has its
0000:              ; 		String DATA in string space. f$=CHR$(7)
0000:              ; 		Will use one byte of string space to store the
0000:              ; 		New one character string created by "CHR$", but
0000:              ; 		The assignment itself will cause no copying since
0000:              ; 		The only pointer at the new string is a
0000:              ; 		Temporary descriptor created by "FRMEVL" which will
0000:              ; 		Go away as soon as the assignment is done.
0000:              ; 		It is the nature of garbage collection that
0000:              ; 		Disallows having two string descriptors point to the same
0000:              ; 		Area in string space. string functions and operators
0000:              ; 		Must proceed as follows:
0000:              ; 			1) Figure out the length of their result.
0000:              
0000:              ; 			2) Call "GETSPA" to find space FOR their
0000:              ; 			Result. the arguments to the function
0000:              ; 			Or operator may change since garbage collection
0000:              ; 			May be invoked. the only thing that can
0000:              ; 			Be saved during the call to "GETSPA" is a pointer
0000:              ; 			To the descriptors of the arguments.
0000:              ; 			3) Construct the result descriptor in "DSCTMP".
0000:              ; 			"GETSPA" returns the location of the available
0000:              ; 			Space.
0000:              ; 			4) Create the new value by copying parts
0000:              ; 			Of the arguments or whatever.
0000:              ; 			5) Free up the arguments by calling "FRETMP".
0000:              ; 			6) Jump to "PUTNEW" to GET the descriptor in
0000:              ; 			"DSCTMP" transferred into a new string temporary.
0000:              
0000:              ; 		The REASON FOR string temporaries is that garbage
0000:              ; 		Collection has to know about all active string descriptors
0000:              ; 		So it knows what is and isn't in use. string temporaries are
0000:              ; 		Used to store the descriptors of string expressions.
0000:              
0000:              ; 		Instead of having an actual value stored in the
0000:              ; 		FAC, and having the value of a temporary result
0000:              ; 		Being saved on the stack, as happens with numeric
0000:              ; 		Variables, strings have the pointer to a string descriptor
0000:              ; 		Stored in the FAC, and it is this pointer
0000:              ; 		That gets saved on the stack by formula evaluation.
0000:              ; 		String functions cannot free their arguments up RIGHT
0000:              ; 		Away since "GETSPA" may force
0000:              ; 		Garbage collection and the argument strings
0000:              ; 		May be over-written since garbage collection
0000:              ; 		Will not be able to find an active pointer to
0000:              ; 		Them. function and operator results are built in
0000:              ; 		"DSCTMP" since string temporaries are allocated
0000:              ; 		(PUTNEW) and deallocated (FRETMP) in a fifo ordering
0000:              ; 		(I.e. a stack) so the new temporary cannot
0000:              ; 		Be set up until the old one(s) are freed. trying
0000:              ; 		To build a result in a temporary after
0000:              ; 		Freeing up the argument temporaries could result
0000:              ; 		In one of the argument temporaries being overwritten
0000:              ; 		Too soon by the new result.
0000:              

