0000:              ; 		At the first location not used by the math-package
0000:              ; 		And [TXTTAB] is set up to point at the NEXT location.
0000:              ; 		This determines where program storage will START.
0000:              ; 		Special checks are made to make sure
0000:              ; 		All questions in "INIT" are answered reasonably, since
0000:              ; 		Once "INIT" finishes, the locations it uses are
0000:              ; 		Used FOR program storage. the last thing "INIT" does is
0000:              ; 		Change location ZERO to be a jump to "READY" instead
0000:              ; 		Of "INIT". once this is done there is no way to restart
0000:              ; 		"INIT".
