          THE "FOR" STATEMENT.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D606:                      .subttl THE "FOR" STATEMENT.
D606:              
D606:              ; A "FOR" entry on the stack has the following format:
D606:              
D606:              ; Low address
D606:              ;	Token (FORTK) 1 byte
D606:              ;	A pointer to the loop variable 2 bytes
D606:              ;	The step 4+ADDPRC bytes
D606:              ;	A byte reflecting the SIGN of the increment 1 byte
D606:              ;	The upper value 4+ADDPRC bytes
D606:              ;	The line number of the "FOR" statement 2 bytes
D606:              ;	A text pointer into the "FOR" statement 2 bytes
D606:              ; High address
D606:              
D606:              ; Total 16+2*ADDPRC bytes.
D606:              
D606:              FOR:
D606: a9 80                LDA     #128                 ;Don't recognize
D608: 85 14                STA     SUBFLG               ;Subscripted variables.
D60A: 20 ca d8             JSR     LET                  ;READ the variable and assign it
D60D:                                                   ;The correct initial value and store
D60D:                                                   ;A pointer to the variable in VARPNT.
D60D: 20 70 d2             JSR     FNDFOR               ;Pntr is in VARPNT, and FORPNT.
D610: d0 17   D617         BNE     NOTOL                ;IF no match, don't eliminate anything.
D612: 8a                   TXA                          ;Make it arithmetical.
D613: 69 0f                ADC     #FORSIZ - 3          ;Eliminate almost all.
D615: aa                   TAX                          ;Note c=1, then pla, pla.
D616: 9a                   TXS                          ;Manifest.
D617:              NOTOL:
D617: 68                   PLA                          ;GET rid of NEWSTT RETURN address
D618: 68                   PLA                          ;In case this is a totally new entry.
D619: a9 09                LDA     #8 + ADDPRC
D61B: 20 e1 d2             JSR     GETSTK               ;Make sure 16 bytes are available.
D61E: 20 2b d8             JSR     DATAN                ;GET a COUNT in [y] of the number of
D621:                                                   ;Chacracters LEFT in the "FOR" statement
D621:                                                   ;[TXTPTR] is unaffected.
D621: 18                   CLC                          ;Prep to add.
D622: 98                   TYA                          ;SAVE it FOR pushing.
D623: 65 ba                ADC     TXTPTR
D625: 48                   PHA
D626: a5 bb                LDA     TXTPTR + 1
D628: 69 00                ADC     #0
D62A: 48                   PHA
D62B:                      PSHWD   CURLIN               ;Put line number on stack.
D62B: a5 79                LDA     CURLIN + 1
D62D: 48                   PHA
D62E: a5 78                LDA     CURLIN
D630: 48                   PHA
D631:                      SYNCHK  TOTK                 ;"To" is necessary.
D631: a9 9d                LDA     #TOTK
D633: 20 5b dd             JSR     SYNCHR
D636: 20 02 dc             JSR     CHKNUM               ;Value must be a number.
D639: 20 ff db             JSR     FRMNUM               ;GET upper value into FAC.
D63C: a5 a6                LDA     FACSGN               ;Pack FAC.
D63E: 09 7f                ORA     #127
D640: 25 a2                AND     FACHO
D642: 85 a2                STA     FACHO                ;Set packed SIGN bit.
D644:                      LDWDI   LDFONE
D644: a9 4f                LDA     #LDFONE & 0o377
D646: a0 d6                LDY     #LDFONE / 0o400

