DB94:                      .subttl THE NEXT CODE IS THE "NEXT CODE"
DB94:              
DB94:              ; A "FOR" entry on the stack has the following format:
DB94:              
DB94:              ; Low address
DB94:              ;	Token (FORTK) 1 byte
DB94:              ;	A pointer to the loop variable 2 bytes
DB94:              ;	The step 4+ADDPRC bytes
DB94:              ;	A byte reflecting the SIGN of the increment 1 byte
DB94:              ;	The upper value (packed) 4+ADDPRC bytes
DB94:              ;	The line number of the "FOR" statement 2 bytes
DB94:              ;	A text pointer into the "FOR" statement 2 bytes
DB94:              ; High address
DB94:              
DB94:              ; Total 16+2*ADDPRC bytes.
DB94:              
DB94:              NEXT:
DB94: d0 9a   DB9A         BNE     GETFOR
