EF1F:                      .subttl ARCTANGENT FUNCTION.
EF1F:                                                   ;Use identities to GET arg between 0 and 1 and then use an
EF1F:                                                   ;Approximation polynomial to compute arctan(x)*
EF1F:              ATN:
EF1F: a5 a6                LDA     FACSGN               ;What is SIGN?
EF21: 48                   PHA                          ;(Meanwhile SAVE FOR later.)
EF22: 10 27   EF27         BPL     ATN1
EF24: 20 51 ed             JSR     NEGOP                ;IF negative, negate FAC.
EF27:                                                   ;Use arctan(x)=-arctan(-x) *
EF27:              ATN1:
EF27: a5 a1                LDA     FACEXP
EF29: 48                   PHA                          ;SAVE this too FOR later.
EF2A: c9 81                CMP     #0o201               ;See IF FAC .ge. 1.0 *
EF2C: 90 35   EF35         BCC     ATN2                 ;It is less than 1.
EF2E:                      LDWDI   FONE                 ;GET pntr to 1.0 *
EF2E: a9 94                LDA     #FONE & 0o377
EF30: a0 e7                LDY     #FONE / 0o400
EF32: 20 e7 e8             JSR     FDIV                 ;Compute reciprocal.
EF35:                                                   ;Use arctan(x)=pi/2-arctan(1/x) *
EF35:              ATN2:
EF35:                      LDWDI   ATNCON               ;Pntr to arctan constants.
EF35: a9 4f                LDA     #ATNCON & 0o377
EF37: a0 ef                LDY     #ATNCON / 0o400
EF39: 20 dd ed             JSR     POLYX
EF3C: 68                   PLA
EF3D: c9 81                CMP     #0o201               ;Was original argument .lt. 1 ?
EF3F: 90 48   EF48         BCC     ATN3                 ;Yes.
EF41:                      LDWDI   PI2
EF41: a9 e7                LDA     #PI2 & 0o377
EF43: a0 ee                LDY     #PI2 / 0o400
EF45: 20 27 e6             JSR     FSUB                 ;Subtract arctagn from pi/2.
EF48:              ATN3:
EF48: 68                   PLA                          ;Was original argument positive?
EF49: 10 4e   EF4E         BPL     ATN4                 ;Yes.
EF4B: 4c 51 ed             JMP     NEGOP                ;IF negative, negate result.
EF4E:              ATN4:
EF4E: 60                   RTS                          ;All done.
